.TH RBAD 8 "2026-11-23" "rbad 0.1.0" "Remote Biometric Authenticator daemon"
.SH NAME
rbad \- Remote Biometric Authenticator daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
rbad [\-\-check] [\-\-state-dir PATH] [\-\-socket PATH]
     [\-\-audit-log PATH] [\-\-bind ADDR] [\-\-port N]
     [\-\-no-mdns] [\-\-mdns-interface NAME]
     [\-\-host-name NAME]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fbrbad\fP is the daemon for the Remote Biometric Authenticator system.
It manages biometric authenticator pairings, handles authentication requests,
and provides a Unix control socket for \fBrba\fP clients.
.PP
The daemon runs as an unprivileged system user (\fBrba\fP) and creates a
Unix domain socket at the path specified by \fB--socket\fP (default:
\fB/run/rba/control.sock\fP when a system install is present, otherwise a
per-user socket under \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rba/control.sock\fP).
.PP
The daemon can be started manually with \fIrbad\fP, or automatically by
\fBrba start-server\fP (user-level) or \fIsystemctl start rbad\fP (system-level).
.PP
The daemon supports the following options:
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fP
Check that the configuration is valid without binding any socket or opening
the audit log. Useful for early validation in scripts.
.TP
\fB\-\-state-dir PATH\fP
Root-only directory holding \fBhost.key\fP, \fBhost.crt\fP and \fBregistry.json\fP.
Default: \fB/var/lib/rba\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket PATH\fP
Unix control socket path. Defaults to \fB/run/rba/control.sock\fP if a
system install exists, otherwise a per-user socket.
.TP
\fB\-\-audit-log PATH\fP
Path to the audit log file. Default: \fB/var/log/rba/audit.log\fP.
.TP
\fB\-\-bind ADDR\fP
TCP bind address in \fBIP:PORT\fP format. Default: loopback only
(\fB0.0.0.0:47123\fP). Exposing on LAN is an explicit deployment decision;
use a firewall to restrict access.
.TP
\fB\-\-port N\fP
TCP port (overrides \fB--bind\fP port). Default: 47123.
.TP
\fB\-\-no-mdns\fP
Disable mDNS advertisement of the control socket.
.TP
\fB\-\-mdns-interface NAME\fP
Specify which interface mDNS should use for advertisement.
.TP
\fB\-\-host-name NAME\fP
Host label shown on the device. Derived from the hostname by default.
.TP
\fB\-\-foreground\fP
Run the daemon in the foreground (useful for debugging).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB/usr/libexec/rbad\fP
Default daemon binary path (system install).
.TP
\fB/var/lib/rba\fP
Default state directory (root-only).
.TP
\fB/var/log/rba\fP
Default audit log directory (root-only).
.TP
\fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rba/control.sock\fP
Per-user control socket (when no system install).
.TP
\fB/etc/systemd/system/rbad.service\fP
Systemd service file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The following exit codes are used:
.TP
\fB0\fP
Success (daemon started or check passed).
.TP
\fB1\fP
Error (configuration invalid, runtime error, socket not available).
.SH SEE ALSO
rba(1), pam_rba(8), systemctl(8)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by burtvadr for the Remote Biometric Authenticator project.